  "_comment": "Controlled genre taxonomy. Open Library subjects are noisy (median 12 per work, 2550 distinct strings per 180 works), so mapping is deliberately conservative: anchored patterns, not greedy substrings. 'strong' patterns carry full confidence; 'weak' patterns only contribute when nothing strong matched. Edit this file and re-run the genre stage; raw_subjects is retained so no re-ingest is needed. Revised after the first full ingest: coverage gaps measured across 788 unmapped works drove looser anchors for poetry/young-adult, much broader technology coverage, bare 'fiction' as a weak literary-fiction signal, and a new art-design genre. raw_subjects is retained precisely so this can be iterated without re-fetching.",
